Another successful journey in my quest to win with all classes and
races on the NAO server. This orc took care of the race part at least;
I figured starting with poison resistance would be handy. Assisted by
an early wand of wishing, I soon had reflection and magic resistance.
Trained daggers to expert and long sword to skilled in hopes of
getting Frost Brand; almost wished for it, but didn't want to break
that conduct. After receiving Grimtooth and Fire Brand (the latter of
which I used for awhile), Frosty was happily mine before the mid-game.

Had lots of pets that died before I had a chance to try to polymorph
them into something more useful than canines and felines. Finally one
survived long enough for me to drag it over a polytrap in the mines;
it became a master lich. I had recently lost a promising orc to touch
of death from a confused pet lich, so was wary, but figured magic
resistance would save me should this happen again. After letting her
kill all the shopkeepers (save Izchak), I was careful to keep Dagmar
the Master Lich (soon Arch Lich) on a different level than me whenever
I donated for protection, so she wouldn't teleport in and kill the
priest. Also found a bag of holding, so I skipped Sokoban.

Around DL 17 I arrived on the upstair to find another arch-lich and
the ghost of a very dead adventurer. Dagmar busied herself teasing the
ghost, while I burned Elbereth and slowly killed the lich (throwing my
stack of +7 daggers helped since archies are both cold and fire
resistant). Helped myself to lots of stuff once I remembered to cancel
the player's cursed bag of holding. Yay helm of brilliance; I might
have wished for one otherwise, as orcs aren't naturally very smart.

Quest was easy since I'd prepared with several cursed scrolls of
teleportation. Left Dagmar in the mines and genocided L h ; and
disenchanters. Ludios yielded spellbooks of identify and magic mapping
- double yay! Cleared the castle, and used more wishes for speed
boots, gauntlets of dexterity, and finally ring of conflict when I was
unable to polypile these after a reasonable amount of time. Eventually
nurse-danced and alchemized up to 450+ HP, which ended up being
overkill, as were the 8 amulets of life saving I collected (none were
used).

Mapped my way through Gehennom; no significant threats. Had to visit
all three altars on Astral, but none of the Riders were much of a
problem. Jumping spell actually helped this time, though I'd only
trained it to Basic. Offered at the last altar and ascended with my
sixth NAO class and fifth race. I've had five wins in the last month,
so clearly I need to get a life. :-P

